7. Documentation consistency

Review and update any descriptions that now contradict the desired interface, particularly:

* docs/systems/input.md
* Relevant comments in js/ui/touch-controls.js
* Relevant comments in js/ui/touch-layout-editor.js
* Relevant comments in js/ui/icons.js
* Relevant test descriptions

The documentation must explain that Defence always uses the shield glyph, Mouvement uses double arrows, and the editor uses neutral icons regardless of character.

8. Acceptance criteria

The work is complete only when:

1. The Jump icon has no horizontal line beneath it.
2. Defence always displays the shield icon, including in the air.
3. The Joystick scheme’s two Mouvement buttons display double directional arrows.
4. Every attack button on the personalization screen displays the correct number of dots.
5. All other personalization controls display universal default icons, never fighter-specific artwork.
6. All attack slots are available for layout editing regardless of selected character.
7. Character-specific attack artwork continues to work normally during gameplay.
8. Existing input behavior, saved layouts, localization, and combat mechanics remain unchanged.
9. Automated tests pass.

9. Final deliverable

Implement the changes directly in the appropriate existing modules.

Keep the patch focused on the interface and avoid unrelated refactoring.

When finished, provide:

* A concise summary of the changes.
* The files modified.
* Any new or updated tests.
* The result of running node --test.
* Confirmation that gameplay mechanics and saved touch layouts are unchanged.

Final goal: Alva’s touch controls should have consistent universal Jump, Defence, and Mouvement icons, while the personalization screen should display a clean, neutral set of buttons that looks the same for every character.
